## Qualification And Cost Boundary

- Use the smallest code change that fixes the reported behavior. Reuse existing mechanisms and
  batch shared fixes, especially #69 with #53.
- Run a quick targeted check for the changed behavior. Add a focused regression test only when a
  short check cannot credibly catch a likely recurrence or state-loss failure.
- Do not make full-suite testing, a release matrix, extended soak, or broad cross-platform
  qualification the default. Expand checks only for an observed failure, concrete data-integrity
  risk, or a separately authorized delivery gate.
- Observe longer-lived behavior during normal local use. Do not hold a local fix idle solely to
  accumulate passive observation time.
- Keep tool and model work bounded. Avoid duplicate investigation and extra planning artifacts
  unless a specific issue cannot be handled directly.

